{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,360p' aristotle_tasks/P59B-mixed-gns-uhf-bridge.md && sed -n '1,280p' reviews/P59A-concrete-pure-mixed-product-data-closeout.md && sed -n '1,280p' reviews/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor-closeout.md && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P55D-regional-concrete-cstar-alpha-closeout.md && sed -n '1,260p' reviews/P56R-regional-cstar-product-state-closeout.md && sed -n '1,220p' PROGRESS.md 2>/dev/null || true && sed -n '1,220p' CONTEXT-LEDGER.md 2>/dev/null || true && if [ -d aristotle_responses/P59B-mixed-gns-uhf-bridge-60d29fa6-bb6c00a3-quarantine ]; then find aristotle_responses/P59B-mixed-gns-uhf-bridge-60d29fa6-bb6c00a3-quarantine -maxdepth 2 -mindepth 1 -printf '%P\\\\n' | sort | head -n 100; fi\"","aggregated_output":"# P59B — mixed GNS/UHF bridge\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1945-1967`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P59B`; Lane `H`.\n- **Predecessors:** P59A and P58, integrated and locally audited.\n- **Gate discharged:** identify the concrete mixed GNS component of P59A with\n  P58's dyadic-UHF weak-closure model and transport its factor/tracial\n  structure.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no pure type-I factor, no regional product\n  transport, no trace/weight dichotomy, and no fresh mixed-factor premise.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/MixedGNSUHFBridge.lean`. Build a unitary or\nstar-equivalence from the actual mixed coordinate algebra/GNS representation\ninside P59A to P58's UHF representation. Use it to transport P58's finite and\ninfinite mixed alternatives and named weak-closure conclusions to P59A's\nmixed representation. Prove the exact statement needed later, not merely that\nboth models are UHF.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nUse only P58's explicit `MixedWeakClosurePremises` where P58 itself uses them,\nand make the coordinate-index identification explicit. Do not add a new mixed\nfactor, mixed trace, equivalence, or normality field.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/MixedGNSUHFBridge.lean`; import P59A and P58.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n`lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedGNSUHFBridge` succeeds, the bridge uses\nactual P58 declarations, and no `sorry`, axiom, or supplied mixed-factor\npremise is introduced.\n# P59A closeout review — concrete pure/mixed product datum\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the packet's stated conditional Lane-H scope; queue may advance.**\n\nAristotle task `f17ae380-7cbe-4e16-8ea3-94d98cb8ef47` is terminal `COMPLETE` in `history/logs/20260810T213056Z-a130d169-tasks.log`. Only its exact archive `aristotle_responses/P59A-concrete-pure-mixed-product-data-a130d169-f17ae380.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `54d09cdca8580fdc5a2d1d37f4db6f4d805e6f46e93acc4fa9db58e33d9ce75b`) was extracted into its named quarantine directory. No build, dependency update, or fetch was run there. The only integrated source is the packet-authorized `AristotleCandidates/ConcretePureMixedProductData.lean`. Its live and quarantine SHA-256 values agree:\n\n```text\n8e646687234146d34a1e27c63eb8c65ddbe9cfc59a025135291e9a932a34b8b6\n```\n\nThe quarantined copies of `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean`, `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean`, and `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` are byte-identical to their live, locally audited counterparts. P57 is used only for its already integrated `ProductGNSData` structure.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `A : AlphaData L I` and `R : A.SourceConcreteRep`, P59A constructs:\n\n- `pureCStar`, `mixedCStar`, `pureEmbedding`, and `mixedEmbedding` as the closed selected-coordinate and complementary-coordinate C-star subalgebras of `R.sourceCStar` and their inclusion star homomorphisms;\n- `pureCStar_mixedCStar_commute` and `pureEmbedding_mixedEmbedding_commute`, derived by closing the verified cross-coordinate Pauli-word commutation relation;\n- `productSpan` and `dense_productSpan`, using the exact split of every finite-stage word and the P55D dense source embedding;\n- `totalStateCLM_mul`, which factors the recovered P56R source state on all pure/mixed elementary products; and\n- the square-positivity conversion `positiveOfStarSq`, positive marginals, `SourceConcreteRep.concreteProductGNSData`, and the branch-uniform `AlphaData.concreteProductGNSData`, with identification lemmas for the total algebra and total state.\n\nThere is no new premise argument. The result inherits only the explicit coordinate-model data already carried by `AlphaData` and `SourceConcreteRep`: the accepted P52/P53/P55D coordinate and concrete-model data, including the named `symplectic` and `stage_surjective` fields. The total state is exactly P56R's `cstarProductStateRecovered`; `ProductStateBound` is not an argument of any P59A declaration. The C-star order used to build Mathlib `PositiveLinearMap`s is explicitly `CStarAlgebra.spectralOrder`.\n\n## Acceptance classification\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The selected/complementary concrete C-star subalgebras, commuting inclusions, norm-dense span of their elementary products, positive unital marginal functionals, product identity, contractivity, and concrete `ProductGNSData` are constructed from P55D/P56R data. |\n| partial | The result is conditional infrastructure relative to the manuscript: it does not construct the underlying local-hyperbolic coordinate/model hypotheses from `main.tex:1925-1967`. |\n| blocked | Completed ITP/GNS factor identification, pure and mixed factor classification, regional factor transport, and trace/weight conclusions remain separate downstream gates. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThus P59A's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. This is not a proof of a completed infinite tensor product, a factor theorem, or a trace/weight theorem.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P59A`, Lane `H`, as declared in both the packet and `PLAN.md`.\n- **Predecessors:** P55D and P56R are integrated, live audited in their respective closeouts, and match the quarantined copies. The integrated P57 supplies only the generic target structure permitted by the packet; it is not used to obtain a factor or trace conclusion.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged exactly: P59A instantiates P57's generic product datum from the P55D/P56R concrete coordinate model rather than adding arbitrary `ProductGNSData`, density, product-state, positivity, or norm-bound fields.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no completed ITP, pure/mixed factor classification, regional factor, normality, trace, or weight theorem.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.ConcretePureMixedProductData` — completed, but Lake has no registered target for this untracked candidate and produced no candidate `.olean`; it is not acceptance evidence by itself.\n- `lake env lean AristotleCandidates/ConcretePureMixedProductData.lean` — passed in the live project; this is the narrow source-level Lean check.\n- Direct live elaboration of P59A together with `#print axioms` for `pureCStar_mixedCStar_commute`, `dense_productSpan`, `totalStateCLM_mul`, `positiveOfStarSq`, both exported datum declarations, and the non-vacuity theorem — passed. Each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Direct live Lean checks of the P55D, P56R, and P57 support modules — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed (existing registered project targets up to date).\n- Declaration-head scan of P59A — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. `git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking issue found. The load-bearing checks were that each finite source word is split into pure and mixed filters at the same stage, the two pairing orientations vanish before commutation is concluded, dense span follows from the actual P55D dense source embedding, and state factorization is extended from words only through closed linear submodules. The positivity conversion explicitly uses the pinned spectral C-star order; it does not replace positivity by an axiom. Compilation and axiom reports validate the Lean artifact, not the inherited coordinate hypotheses or later operator-algebraic claims.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P59A candidate, its exact archive, quarantine extraction, and this review. All pre-existing modified and untracked plan, packet, candidate, and review files were preserved. No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, archive build, dependency update, or dependency fetch occurred.\n\n# P58 closeout review — mixed UHF factor classification\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated mixed-sector, conditional Lane-H scope; queue may\nadvance.**\n\nAristotle task `ed55ef94-0313-4123-9cc0-b00ffdb465aa` was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P58-mixed-uhf-hyperfinite-factor.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`6a9c6e453986cbacfed106b03db592f946fd61c13acb976a9b9da8f4c3c7c7b5`) and\nextracted without building, updating, or fetching dependencies at\n`aristotle_responses/P58-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p58-3px4hkyb_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project. Its quarantine and live SHA-256 values agree:\n`5dbf9ff8c35035c94b37804435793102cb0c59f88c7a39e2746c32274fc67d20`.\nThe archive and extraction remain raw response records. No manuscript file was\nchanged.\n\n## Source and exact declarations\n\nThe source basis is the narrow claim in `main.tex:1945-1967`, specifically the\nfinite maximally-mixed matrix alternative and the infinite maximally-mixed\nhyperfinite-II1 assertion at lines 1964-1966. This packet formalizes only the\nproject-local dyadic mixed sector; it neither establishes the preceding GNS\ntensor splitting nor transports its result to the manuscript's regional algebra.\n\nThe new module's load-bearing declarations are:\n\n- `qubitMatrixStarEquiv` (line 197) and\n  `qubitTensorTrace_eq_normalizedTrace` (line 213), identifying the `n`-qubit\n  algebra with `M_(2^n)(C)` and its trace with normalized matrix trace;\n- `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor` (line 291), whose explicit fields are\n  the star equivalence, positivity of `2^n`, normalized-trace identity,\n  traciality, faithfulness, and algebraic scalar centre;\n- `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter` (line 314) and\n  `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra` (line 331), the algebraic infinite-limit\n  statements;\n- `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain` (line 410), an increasing dense chain of\n  finite matrix subalgebras in the P54 concrete C-star model;\n- `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 683) and\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter` (line 725), direct\n  matrix-unit proofs of trivial centre for each finite-stage generated concrete\n  von Neumann algebra;\n- `mixedVonNeumann` (line 739), defined as the von Neumann algebra generated\n  by `UHFConcreteCStar`; and\n- the conditional `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` (line 840).\n\nThe last theorem uses exactly the three fields of\n`MixedWeakClosurePremises` (lines 798-811): traciality of `uhfVectorState` on\nthe weak closure, faithfulness there, and `HasTrivialOperatorCenter` of that\nweak closure. `IsHyperfiniteFiniteFactorModel` (line 814) is explicitly a\nproject-local feature predicate: factorhood, a vector-normal faithful tracial\nstate, a matricial chain, and unbounded matrix sizes. It is **not** a proof of\nthe Murray-von Neumann/Connes uniqueness/classification theorem for the\nhyperfinite II1 factor.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The finite mixed stage is star-isomorphic to `M_(2^n)(C)` with normalized faithful tracial functional and scalar centre. The algebraic UHF limit has scalar centre and is not a finite matrix algebra. In the P54 representation, finite matrix stages form a monotone dense C-star-level chain; each individual stage's generated von Neumann algebra has trivial centre by the local matrix-unit proof. The conditional theorem assembles the stated project-local finite-factor model. |\n| partial | Infinite weak-closure traciality, faithfulness, and factorhood are not proved; they are the three named fields above. The module's `IsVectorNormal` is a project-local single-vector-functional predicate, not a formalized Mathlib sigma-weak continuity theory. No canonical hyperfinite-II1 classification/isomorphism is formalized. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks P58's stated gate, because the packet expressly permits an analytic factoriality/classification bridge only as an explicit conditional interface. Those analytic premises remain open for any later use. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe packet's mathematical target is met at its stated scope. The alternate\nroute is a direct finite-matrix/matrix-unit construction plus a C-star-level\nmatricial approximation, rather than an unproved weak-closure transfer. It\nadds exactly the three `MixedWeakClosurePremises`; it does not silently weaken\nthe finite result or promote the conditional infinite result to a theorem of\nthe manuscript.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P58, Lane H — correct.\n- **Predecessors:** P54 is integrated, compiled, and audited in\n  `reviews/P54-uhf-reference-representation-closeout.md`. The imports\n  `Formalization.DyadicTensorTower`, P54's\n  `UHFReferenceRepresentation`, and the pre-existing local bicommutant core\n  are byte-identical between the quarantine snapshot and live checkout. The\n  bicommutant core is supporting infrastructure, not an undeclared later Lane-H\n  package dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the finite mixed matrix alternative is\n  proved, and the infinite alternative supplies a checked matrix approximation\n  with all weak-closure/factor/classification gaps isolated as named premises.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. The candidate contains no\n  regional alpha transport, pure-sector classification, spatial product\n  factorhood, regional factor claim, or final trace/weight theorem. Its\n  finite-stage factor statements and conditional mixed weak-closure model are\n  confined to the P54 dyadic reference representation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor` — passed (8038\n  jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.UHFReferenceRepresentation AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor Formalization` — passed (8089 jobs) in the live project.\n- `lake build` — passed in the live project; no work was required after the\n  focused build.\n- `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.olean AristotleCandidates/MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` — passed in the live project, producing the importable cache used by the axiom check.\n- `#print axioms` for `qubitTensorPower_isMixedMatrixFactor`,\n  `qubitUHF_hasScalarCenter`, `qubitUHF_not_matrixAlgebra`,\n  `uhfConcreteCStar_isMatricialChain`,\n  `matrixRange_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `mixedStage_vonNeumannGenerated_trivialCenter`,\n  `uhfVectorState_isVectorNormal`, and\n  `mixedVonNeumann_isHyperfiniteFiniteFactor` — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate and its three direct imports —\n  no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Direct-import SHA-256 comparisons, candidate quarantine/live SHA-256\n  comparison, and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked the finite normalization\nagainst the actual recursive matrix equivalence; that the algebraic scalar-\ncentre proof first reduces an arbitrary limit el